    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0487" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Generalissimo Chiang to President Roosevelt </hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d160-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-29">May 29, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am in receipt of your telegram of May 25<anchor n="2" xml:id="d160-f2"/> and
                    wish to express my deep appreciation of the measures you have taken to
                    strengthen the United States Air Force in China, and to increase the capacity of
                    air transport to China.</p>
                <p>In regard to <hi rendition="#small-caps">Anakim</hi> I feel assured that you
                    already possess a comprehensive and well-prepared plan of strategy, and that you
                    are resolutely determined on pressing it forward to victory. I feel particularly
                    grateful for the patience and courage with which you have resolved the many
                    difficulties arising on all sides so that <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Anakim</hi> can go through. I venture to make a few supplementary
                    observations which I have asked Dr. T. V. Soong to submit to you for your
                        consideration.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d160-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chiang Kai-shek</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d160-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d160-f1-content">
                <p>This message appears to have been handed to Hopkins by Foreign Minister
                    Soong.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d160-f2" n="2" xml:id="d160-f2-content">
                <p>No telegram direct from Roosevelt to Chiang has been found. Chiang’s reference is
                    presumably to the message that Roosevelt gave Soong on the afternoon of May 25,
                    1943; see the editorial note, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg208">p. 208</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d160-f3" n="3" xml:id="d160-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
